LF. n1-r1 spends 285 lines on meridian.py against n1-r2's 134 — MORE THAN DOUBLE on the vendor client, which is precisely what tier C grades from the request trace: cursor paging, fetching every page, honouring Retry-After. n1-r1's api.py is SMALLER at 160 lines against 187. So the better app wrote more of the hard part and less of the boilerplate, while F569 measured n1-r2 making MORE tool calls and 53% MORE write/edit operations. MORE CHURN, LESS PRODUCT, IN THE PART THAT MATTERS. ⚠️ n IS SIX TREES FOR THE PREVALENCE CLAIM AND TWO APPS FOR THE CONTRAST. The line-count story is one pair and I am not turning it into a rule; what is solid is the 1-of-6 prevalence, which is what actually decides whether to build the detector, and the answer is NO. ⚠️ AND FIVE MORE TREES ARE NOW AVAILABLE TO READ that I had wrongly written off — the contrast can be widened without waiting for a single new cell. ⇒ L378 MEASURE PREVALENCE BEFORE BUILDING THE DETECTOR, AND LIST THE DIRECTORY BEFORE DECLARING IT GONE - ONE COMMAND KILLED A DETECTOR I DID NOT NEED AND HANDED BACK FIVE ARTEFACTS I HAD ALREADY WRITTEN OFF TWICE IN WRITING
